Upon satisfactory completion of this course, students will be able to:

1. Understand the bonding models and how they can explain molecules' properties;
2. Interpret simple NMR (nuclear magnetic resonance), IR (infrared), and mass spectra of organic compounds;
3. Explain the mechanism of certain types of chemical reactions;
4. Critically analyze relevant published studies in organic chemistry;
5. Perform basic organic lab’s procedures and write lab reports.
